<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:19Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia bans two French lawmakers and two journalists from entry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9226846459234ddde32857ebcacdaa36aee09f517001a6ac6b9eae0a7c0aae3f</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:58:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry--647f8165ba44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry" /><summary type="html">Moscow on Wednesday said it was banning two French journalists and two French lawmakers from entering Russia in response to Paris's expulsion of pro-Russian TV commentator Xenia Fedorova earlier this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Armistice Day in France: Commemorating the end of World War I</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df696fcf221ca9d415ee8f64c7df11a858745aebcaa9c0f6c3c7f4810447305</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:57:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-armistice-day-in-france-commemorating-the-end-of-world-war-i--1302880ba7fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-armistice-day-in-france-commemorating-the-end-of-world-war-i" /><summary type="html">With less than six months to go before the presidential election, the 11 November commemorations have taken on a political hue. On Wednesday, Emmanuel Macron presided over his final ceremony in Paris, whilst the candidates vying to succeed him made their positions clear.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: General strike over housing costs before national election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dcaafcf1068f1db6ee2384df09376dc27fd0bd3ae1103f9bc1cae60b5da006c</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:54:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election--d795ce513ad5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election" /><summary type="html">Millions of Spanish workers shut down businesses and public transportation in a protest on Wednesday over housing costs that the government hopes to leverage before a national election later this month. The walkout — under the slogan “Salaries. Housing. Prices.” — was the first general strike in Spain in 14 years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exclusive: EU's Kallas says US 'can't negotiate on our behalf' on lifting Russia sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c0c3f2435a61381cf6f1fdf44d5f020466807a554c3598e92403d69de40b93b</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions--7f31e05dcc4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, the EU's top diplomat Kaja Kallas discusses the war in Ukraine, the situation in the Middle East and a possible change in US President Donald Trump's foreign policy following the US midterm elections. The former Estonian prime minister, who is now the European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, also reaffirms the EU's position as a major player on the global geopolitical stage.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Charlotte Gainsbourg brings pioneering French lawyer Gisèle Halimi to the screen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b9f96dc4f03354991cef5423d35501171fa18de73e81f212cbcd439a706f69b</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:13:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261111-charlotte-gainsbourg-brings-pioneering-french-lawyer-gis_le-halimi-to-the-screen--15609dd4243d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261111-charlotte-gainsbourg-brings-pioneering-french-lawyer-gis%C3%A8le-halimi-to-the-screen" /><summary type="html">New French film "Women on trial" revisits the landmark case in 1972 that paved the way for abortion legislation in France. Critic Manon Kerjean tells us why performances from Charlotte Gainsbourg and Cécile de France carry this powerful courtroom drama and how its directors recreated the tension of a high-profile social and legal battle.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Behind Georges Larnicol's creative spin on Breton specialty kouign-amann</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c717f167d4e7ad8eef3efa71887fa1b7c6cbed5df017128d4dccdaa810de51a</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T14:05:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261111-tt-behind-georges-larnicol-s-creative-spin-on-kouign-amann--5bf30f3a0c08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261111-tt-behind-georges-larnicol-s-creative-spin-on-kouign-amann" /><summary type="html">From a traditional Breton specialty to an imaginative, bite-sized creation, in Entre Nous we explore how French pastry chef Georges Larnicol has reinvented the famous kouign-amann while preserving its Breton identity. He tells us what makes the pastry so special and why it is much loved around the world.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>UNICEF head Catherine Russell: 'We're all committed to the importance of children'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de9a140b8dcd808ed9fdac36bcdda5b62b1c345200df252681e21660b8d11dbf</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:49:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261111-unicef-head-catherine-russell-we-re-all-committed-to-the-importance-of-children--011117256e24.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261111-unicef-head-catherine-russell-we-re-all-committed-to-the-importance-of-children" /><summary type="html">More than 50 countries, 20 non-governmental and philanthropic organisations and a series of multinational companies are pledging this week to put children's rights at the heart of their policies and actions. A pact is being agreed upon at the Paris Peace Forum, where the rights of children are taking centre stage.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Aneto, one of southern Europe's largest glaciers, is melting away</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bccdae5b6af4b71871b06f3436d6af6bccb4c8e383a807b02859c6846a5d4255</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away--7bca17aca8fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away" /><summary type="html">Within a decade, one of the largest glaciers in southern Europe will have disappeared. Aneto, the highest peak of the Spanish Pyrenees, is melting at a spectacular rate. Its demise is another sign of global warming and has much to teach glaciologists. FRANCE 24's Maude Petit-Jové, Mathilde Lopinski and Sarah Morris report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Patrick Bury: 'It’s going to cost a lot of money to repair the systems.'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2220cabc6bb82a7241e496722c25682ca3e2db23a10516b694759999862a3f6</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict--d7020f165247.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict" /><summary type="html">Patrick Bury, Senior associate professor in warfare and counterterrorism at University of Bath, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>US House votes to derail impeachment of Defense Secretary Hegseth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc14c60300fc5aeacbb38310241954f7ee99e527e7a0e8c98cb160b49f0fd57e</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:17:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-house-votes-to-derail-impeachment-of-defense-secretary-hegseth--b2d11278e1a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-house-votes-to-derail-impeachment-of-defense-secretary-hegseth" /><summary type="html">Republicans in ​the US House ​of Representatives banded together on Tuesday ​to ‌derail ⁠aneffort to impeach ‌Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Fraser Jackson, our correspondant in Washington DC, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Violent clashes near the Sudanese border: At least 65 dead in western Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a00bed4c257c7cfd49afa2e0997dd645db64198891fb0e903636adf73ae978a9</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:07:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/violent-clashes-near-the-sudanese-border-at-least-65-dead-in-western-ethiopia--6607f86e7871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/violent-clashes-near-the-sudanese-border-at-least-65-dead-in-western-ethiopia" /><summary type="html">Tom Canetti, our correspondant in Ethiopia, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK comedian David Walliams accused of grooming and sexual harassment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c35d9f8f08707cb4f62b8ef7f7bdf8a947523edfdae09b71d3441b3620170812</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment--5fccf1ffbe7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, November 11: Spanish and French papers discuss protests in the two countries. An investigation by The Guardian and ITV accuses comedian David Walliams of "preying on young women for sex". Finally, a Doberman sensed something was wrong with a baby. It may have saved his life.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>'Welcome Home': Peru awaits Pope Leo's emotional 'homecoming'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e287ed336a6da71c800d4857a046420cf671da985b2811f1785c18366504d35</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:53:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/welcome-home-peru-awaits-pope-leo-s-emotional-homecoming--c0f157d7b90d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/welcome-home-peru-awaits-pope-leo-s-emotional-homecoming" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo will wrap ​up his visit to Argentina on Wednesday during his 12-day South America tour, with a final event expected to draw millions, before traveling to Peru in an emotional homecoming for the first Peruvian citizen to lead the Catholic Church.</summary></entry><entry><title>France marks Armistice Day : Macron attends commemorative ceremony</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55769af4b2f9cd5607f48c9f810efe7c007d362ec6a1146172facb7a39eab806</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:36:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-marks-armistice-day-macron-attends-commemorative-ceremony--34e92b2a25b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-marks-armistice-day-macron-attends-commemorative-ceremony" /><summary type="html">Macron attends Armistice Day commemoration ceremony at the Arc de Triomphe.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eisenkot quickly targets Netanyahu's legacy in new Israeli parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8205f7dbf9c8b3e9c2a9887bbd17a7b757d732d5cf18cd21b2bf886d228639ee</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:29:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eisenkot-quickly-targets-netanyahu-s-legacy-in-new-israeli-parliament--38561be2e3bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eisenkot-quickly-targets-netanyahu-s-legacy-in-new-israeli-parliament" /><summary type="html">Israeli ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot and his allies launched a legislative onslaught against caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's legacy on Tuesday, as a new parliament convened in a heated first session.</summary></entry><entry><title>EU ready for 'united response' after France blames Iran for fridge hacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:454fe7c0885f7e50d7183b9e47dfa634da48c88ed9449d4945bef7ac9d62da94</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:16:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-ready-for-united-response-after-france-blames-iran-for-fridge-hacks--0f6021e21fcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-ready-for-united-response-after-france-blames-iran-for-fridge-hacks" /><summary type="html">The EU said Tuesday it would look to provide a "swift and united response" after France blamed Iran for a cyberattack on hundreds of supermarket fridges.</summary></entry><entry><title>'France has some of the cleanest electricity in the world, but we're not using enough of it'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32ab94d7ac5896cd9b9f52b35e5bab9e3c10bb8889fdef282365b0cfa00860fb</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:12:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-has-some-of-the-cleanest-electricity-in-the-world-but-we-re-not-using-enough-of-it--1cd5ed26d44a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-has-some-of-the-cleanest-electricity-in-the-world-but-we-re-not-using-enough-of-it" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Thierry Bros, energy &amp; climate expert and Professor of Science and Economics at Sciences Po. As geopolitical conflicts unsettle global energy markets and governments struggle to reconcile climate commitments with economic and security imperatives, the answer lies in a fundamental reconsideration of the sequence of climate policy. "Electrification first," he argues, acknowledging that this "doesn't necessarily mean clean electricity." His argument is grounded in a critical assessment of international climate diplomacy and European energy policy. "We've seen many COPs, and they've all failed," he contends, questioning the effectiveness of ambitious targets that have yet to deliver the necessary structural transformation. In his view, electrification offers a more pragmatic route than some of the technological priorities previously championed by European policymakers.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴Italy: At least 300 schools evacuated after email bomb alerts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4f299e85ccda6c7024c1b5141709467b7c915bd18ccb86e5df27123ec4cebc4</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:59:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats--967169548911.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats" /></entry><entry><title>Wave of hoax bomb threats sent to schools in UK, Ireland and Italy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bae129934047a682eb3bcd98787c3d4a949907a724fea94c2698ce82b1c02759</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats--967169548911.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of schools in the UK, Italy and the Republic of Ireland received a "generic" threatening email on Wednesday now being treated as a hoax by authorities. Italy earlier evacuated roughly 300 schools over the perceived threat.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo to end Argentina tour with outdoor mass before Peru 'homecoming'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3efbf919bd5e66812d1a69cc74a6588bac44383808f1b76f26943990760616c</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:50:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-to-end-argentina-tour-with-large-outdoor-mass-before-emotional-peru-homecoming--6a3146ea450a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-to-end-argentina-tour-with-large-outdoor-mass-before-emotional-peru-homecoming" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo will conclude his three-day visit to Argentina Wednesday with an outdoor mass expected to draw millions before continuing his tour of South America by travelling to Peru, where he once served as a missionary. The pontiff plans to deliver a speech in front of Peruvian President Keiko Fujimori, whose election earlier this year was marred ‌by fraud accusations and vote-counting delays.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Russia, Ukraine start second day of US-led talks: Kyiv lead negotiator</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26135fc23f26f2202cce02ca28e3533d166f0af75ca4128ac4c0eba301ed7399</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:42:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator--ce553d61579f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine have resumed US-mediated talks in Abu Dhabi for a second day, Kyiv's chief negotiator Rustem Umerov said on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>French journalist Christophe Gleizes marks 500 days in Algerian jail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8de998f5acf1fdb4d00aabb034c34c6511e8082274acc9aa53a04b13dbca0aa2</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:40:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-journalist-christophe-gleizes-marks-500-days-in-algerian-jail--460bfcbe4732.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-journalist-christophe-gleizes-marks-500-days-in-algerian-jail" /><summary type="html">Having been detained for 500 days in an Algerian prison on charges of “glorifying terrorism”, French journalist Christophe Gleizes continues to serve a seven-year sentence despite an intense campaign by his family and friends and the football world. While awaiting a presidential pardon, his supporters are stepping up their media campaign to secure his release. FRANCE 24 spoke with his friend Pierre de la Saussay.</summary></entry><entry><title>Second day of Web Summit cancelled as Storm Charles puts Portugal on high alert</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0880c13b1e20fa2087463f77529fc3a5b50dbc8dd209b22580ac094062c8f924</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:37:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261111-second-day-of-web-summit-cancelled-as-storm-charles-puts-portugal-on-high-alert--dd22d9a5b073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261111-second-day-of-web-summit-cancelled-as-storm-charles-puts-portugal-on-high-alert" /><summary type="html">Portuguese authorities strongly advised organisers of the Web Summit to cancel events this Wednesday because of risks of tidal flooding and severe disruption to public transport. Storm Charles is expected to be at its most dangerous on Wednesday afternoon, with winds reaching up to 120 km/h and potentially very dangerous wind gusts as well.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Angry Nemo: Clownfish becoming more agressive because of climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91484b6d1009761ad17baade819bd288a6d41a9985df4ae65b887e2db9bc845f</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:36:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-angry-nemo-clown-fish-becoming-more-agressive-because-of-climate-change--c45f9c6bf440.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-angry-nemo-clown-fish-becoming-more-agressive-because-of-climate-change" /><summary type="html">Listen to Theresa Rueger, Senior Lecturer in Tropical Marine Biology.</summary></entry></feed>
